WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:08.570
<i>When even drinking warm milk or counting 
to one hundred won't help me fall asleep...</i>

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:12.700
Momo-kun!

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.530
Nino-chan!

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.530
Let's sing!

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:22.160
<i>I sing a song with my next-door 
neighbor, Momo-kun.</i>

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:27.810
<i>Twinkle, twinkle, little star</i>

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:32.550
<i>How I wonder what you are</i>

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:37.050
<i>Up above the world so high</i>

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:42.180
<i>Like a diamond in the sky</i>

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.020
Press 
Button 
to Cross

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:46.520
<i>Twinkle, twinkle, little star</i>

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:52.030
<i>How I wonder what you are</i>

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.420
<i>When I sing with Momo-kun, I'm unstoppable.</i>

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:26.950
♭02 God, I Pray That Alice's Love Will Never Be Realized

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:27.470
Tomorrow's the start of second grade, Momo.

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:29.770
I hope we're in the same class, Nino.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:32.380
Look how pretty the moon is.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.820
Hey, Nino. My parents have 
been fighting a lot lately...

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.120
Let's sing!

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:46.190
<i>Twinkle, twinkle, little star</i>

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:47.810
Listen when someone's talking to you.

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:50.690
<i>How I wonder what you are</i>

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:55.570
<i>Up above the world so high</i>

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:55.170
<i>When I sing with Momo, I'm unstoppable.</i>

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:58.740
How have things been at your house 
since we started fourth grade?

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:00.890
Same as ever. Fighting nonstop.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:05.450
It'll be funny if my mom, Riko, 
goes loco and gets a divorce, though.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:06.300
Huh?

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:08.450
It's a pun.

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:10.150
You're supposed to laugh.

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:11.730
Wow, embarrassing!

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:15.290
You two are going home holding hands again!

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:17.920
You're the one who should be embarrassed.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:22.380
Don't be jealous just 'cause there are no 
girls who'll hold your hand. Pathetic.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.420
Sakaki, you jerk!

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:25.300
Stupid Baldy.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.440
<i>When I'm with Momo...</i>

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.100
The fireworks show is coming up soon.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:45.240
Yeah.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:46.120
We're going, right?

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:48.310
Yeah!

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:53.870
<i>Twinkle, twinkle, little star</i>

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:59.130
<i>How I wonder what you are.</i>

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:58.530
<i>When I'm with Momo, I'm unstoppable.</i>

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:11.980
<i>Twinkle, twinkle, little star</i>

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:13.800
Arisugawa, your voice is so annoying!

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:14.170
<i>How I wonder—</i>

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:17.820
I can't sing because Arisugawa is so loud.

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:19.000
He has a point...

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:21.070
She puts too much force into it.

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:25.030
Also, stop singing so loudly 
on the way to and from school.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:27.490
It makes me embarrassed to be your classmate.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:37.580
Momo.

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:42.440
Wh-What's your problem? 
We're in class right now.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:45.630
Nino's voice is annoying? Are you crazy?

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:47.840
Huh? What are you talking about?!

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:50.740
Y-You two are the crazy ones!

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:52.410
What did you say?!

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:53.560
<i>Crazy?</i>

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:53.830
It's true!

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:54.640
Try saying that again!

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:02.030
These are the best seats in the house.

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:06.240
Hey, Momo...

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:10.550
Is it bad for me to sing?

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:16.240
The kids at school and my 
mom tell me it's annoying.

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:17.930
That I'm a nuisance.

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:20.130
You're fine just the way you are.

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:21.430
Huh?

00:05:22.270 --> 00:05:23.570
Just sing.

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:26.790
It's not bad, you're not a nuisance, 
and it's not annoying.

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:29.550
You're fine just the way you are.

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:40.440
<i>Momo...</i>

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:42.930
Nino.

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:46.120
If we can't see each other anymore...

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:48.790
I hope, one day, we can 
use your song as a guide

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:50.410
to find each other again.

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:53.390
Nino?

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:58.070
<i>Twinkle, twinkle, little star</i>

00:05:58.070 --> 00:06:02.540
<i>How I wonder what you are</i>

00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:00.040
Listen when someone's talking to you.

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:02.540
<i>Momo... Momo...</i>

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:07.620
<i>Up above the world so high</i>

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:04.040
<i>Momo!</i>

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:12.670
<i>Like a diamond in the sky</i>

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:20.560
Momo!

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:24.450
Is he already asleep?

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:39.430
Momo! Wake up!

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:41.180
Nino.

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:43.280
Mom?

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:50.300
Nino, Momo-kun moved away.

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:51.760
He moved?

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:54.200
Where? Why?

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:55.650
Will I never see him again?

00:06:56.060 --> 00:07:00.270
No, I'm sure you'll see him again one day.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:03.270
<i>Momo... Is it true?</i>

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:06.410
<i>When are you going to come home?</i>

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:09.030
<i>When will I see you again?</i>

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:15.490
<i>He's not here again today.</i>

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:19.830
It's so much quieter when 
you're not singing, Arisugawa.

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:23.170
I'm glad Sakaki isn't around anymore!

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:41.350
Press 
Button 
to Cross

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:43.750
<i>Momo!</i>

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:47.250
Momo... Momo! Momo!

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:49.110
Momo! Momo!

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:50.740
Momo!

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:55.250
<i>Momo, can't you hear me?</i>

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:57.790
<i>Please open your window.</i>

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.540
<i>Sing with me, Momo.</i>

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:02.730
<i>Momo, if you're not here with me...</i>

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:10.830
Nino!

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:17.760
<i>Momo, if you're not here with me, 
I can't even breathe.</i>

00:08:18.770 --> 00:08:22.230
Arisugawa-san, where did Sakaki-kun move to?

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:25.720
Are you listening or ignoring me?

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:28.500
And why are you wearing a mask? 
Do you have a cold?

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:29.320
Stop it!

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:36.430
S-Sorry.

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:39.030
<i>It's suffocating.</i>

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:40.290
<i>I can't breathe.</i>

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:43.790
<i>I'm suffocating! Suffocating! Suffocating!</i>

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:45.400
<i>I feel like I'm gonna scream!</i>

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:50.550
What are you doing?!

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:54.800
<i>This is...</i>

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:03.020
Milk

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:03.020
<i>That milk carton is huge.</i>

00:09:03.670 --> 00:09:04.770
<i>And...</i>

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:06.770
Your eyelashes are so long.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:10.070
Huh? Who cares about that?! 
Watch where you're stepping!

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:14.600
The musical score I worked 
so hard to write is ruined!

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:19.410
I've never seen such a beautiful song before.

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:24.430
Wh-What do you know, anyway?!

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:30.290
<i>I wish Momo could hear this right now!</i>

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:37.680
I found it. My voice.

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:38.760
Huh?

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:40.400
What's your name?

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:42.490
A-Arisugawa Nino.

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:44.640
Too long! I'm calling you Alice!

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:47.720
I'm Yuzu. I'm here every Wednesday.

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:50.270
I'm going to write the next part 
of this song. Come if you want.

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:58.740
<i>Just now, it wasn't hard to breathe.
It was just like before.</i>

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:00.510
<i>I sang!</i>

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:05.620
We can use your song as a guide
to find each other again.

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:09.730
<i>If I keep singing here, 
maybe I can see Momo again.</i>

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:19.690
Eyelashes!

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:24.550
Who's that supposed to be? My name's Yuzu.

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:29.070
Yuzu-kun, what grade are you in? 
What school? I'm in fourth grade.

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:31.940
You can just call me Yuzu. And fifth grade.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:34.980
But I don't go to any school.

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:36.850
Because you drink too much milk?

00:10:36.850 --> 00:10:39.020
The milk has nothing to do with it!

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:39.860
More importantly...

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:41.610
I've written more of that song.

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:45.670
Sing, Alice.

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:47.660
I've waited all week to hear it.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:57.550
<i>It happened again.</i>

00:10:58.070 --> 00:11:00.740
<i>That suffocating feeling is melting away.</i>

00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:09.230
Hey, do you think this song will reach Momo?

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:10.820
Momo? Who's that?

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:12.760
My next-door neighbor who moved.

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:15.440
Ever since Momo left, 
I feel like I'm suffocating.

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:18.320
I feel like I'll scream if 
I don't keep that mask on.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:23.240
<i>This Momo girl must be a really 
important friend to her.</i>

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:27.830
But when I sing your song, I don't 
feel like I'm suffocating anymore.

00:11:28.590 --> 00:11:31.890
Then I guess I can write you more music.

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:33.460
Why do you write music?

00:11:33.850 --> 00:11:35.500
Listen when someone's talking to you!

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:41.810
I wrote this song to sing myself.

00:11:42.370 --> 00:11:43.650
But I can't sing anymore.

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:45.640
Really? Why?

00:11:46.150 --> 00:11:48.480
I won't sing anymore.

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:52.140
Because if I sing, I'll turn 
into foam and disappear.

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:55.000
<i>I'm the opposite.</i>

00:11:55.490 --> 00:11:57.770
<i>I'll disappear if I don't sing.</i>

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:02.150
<i>I can't breathe if I don't sing.</i>

00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:07.590
<i>Momo, can you still not hear my voice?</i>

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:11.540
<i>Momo, when will I see you again?</i>

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:20.500
I heard the Sakakis were so riddled 
with debt that they skipped town.

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:24.390
Then I guess we won't see them 
around these parts again.

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:25.890
Mom!

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:29.140
Mom, what does "skipping town" mean?

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:33.100
They're lying when they say 
I'll never see Momo again, right?

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:35.200
Mom!

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:40.640
Nino, I have something I've been 
holding on to from Momo-kun.

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:44.200
It's a letter to you.

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:46.320
Dear Nino,

00:12:47.050 --> 00:12:50.080
Thank you for singing with me.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:51.710
<i>There was no point.</i>

00:12:51.710 --> 00:12:53.460
We'll never see each other again...

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:55.680
<i>No matter how loudly I sang...</i>

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:57.630
But I hope you'll be well.

00:12:58.220 --> 00:13:00.460
<i>There was no point at all!</i>

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:09.930
Alice! Alice!

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:12.220
What's wrong, Alice?

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:24.840
I won't sing.

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:28.910
I'll turn into foam and disappear.

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:32.800
<i>Yuzu...</i>

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:37.420
<i>I really do feel like I'm going to melt away.</i>

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:42.450
<i>My heart, and every other part of me...</i>

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:50.590
What happened, Alice?

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:54.510
It's okay. I'm here for you.

00:13:56.700 --> 00:13:58.780
They said I'll never see Momo again.

00:13:58.780 --> 00:14:00.940
The girl that you said moved away?

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:04.070
He even told me that he hoped 
we'd find each other again!

00:14:04.270 --> 00:14:07.110
If I can never see Momo again, 
I won't sing anymore!

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:10.200
I'll never sing again.

00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:11.990
Ever.

00:14:13.390 --> 00:14:15.700
Come on! You like that guy, don't you?

00:14:17.020 --> 00:14:20.580
Then you have to believe you'll 
see him again and keep singing.

00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:23.460
Believe your song will reach 
him and keep singing.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:28.470
If you do that, I'm sure you'll see
him someday, in some way.

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:32.900
If you feel like screaming again, 
you can just sing my song.

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:33.850
<i>Yuzu...</i>

00:14:34.030 --> 00:14:37.850
And if you end up screaming anyway, 
I guess I could sing with you.

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:38.980
<i>Really?</i>

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:43.310
And if you end up going somewhere 
far away, I guess I could go find you.

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:44.940
<i>Really?</i>

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:47.860
After all, there's no way 
I could miss your voice.

00:14:53.860 --> 00:14:55.270
I made a mark on your neck.

00:14:58.240 --> 00:15:00.120
You should go home for now.

00:15:06.750 --> 00:15:08.670
So Momo's a guy?

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:13.010
Arisugawa, I saw what you did yesterday.

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:14.510
Arisugawa

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:14.510
Eyelashes

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:19.230
You were hugging some girly boy 
and singing some stupid song.

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:20.690
What's your problem, Baldy?!

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:23.300
Don't make fun of Yuzu or his song!

00:15:23.300 --> 00:15:25.940
Because it's a really, really great song!

00:15:26.270 --> 00:15:28.430
It's a song that'll reach Momo!

00:15:28.430 --> 00:15:32.290
Huh? Sakaki? You don't 
even know where he went!

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:34.300
There's no way it'll reach him.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:37.340
<i>I-It won't reach him?</i>

00:15:37.340 --> 00:15:41.390
Why don't you try it out and see? 
Right here and now!

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:45.610
<i>Huh?</i>

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:52.090
<i>I'm trembling so much, I can't 
move or even open my mouth.</i>

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:54.820
Believe your song will reach 
him and keep singing.

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:57.020
If you do that, you'll see him again.

00:15:58.760 --> 00:16:01.480
<i>Yuzu... Sorry.</i>

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:07.230
<i>It's Wednesday, but Yuzu isn't here.</i>

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:10.960
<i>They could tell.</i>

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:14.990
<i>They knew I couldn't believe 
in what you told me.</i>

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:18.330
<i>They said that's why I couldn't sing.</i>

00:16:23.570 --> 00:16:24.630
<i>Yuzu...</i>

00:16:26.690 --> 00:16:30.010
After all, there's no way 
I could miss your voice.

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:35.390
You told me to sing, didn't you, Baldy?

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:38.940
I'll sing for you, just like you asked.

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:53.430
<i>Reach him.</i>

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:57.560
<i>Both Yuzu...</i>

00:16:58.590 --> 00:16:59.830
<i>and Momo.</i>

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:03.750
<i>Because I believe I'll see 
you both again for sure.</i>

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:06.750
<i>I'm going to believe and keep on singing.</i>

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:10.230
<i>Reach him!</i>

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:18.260
Bye-bye, Alice

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:20.390
<i>It was probably...</i>

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:23.860
<i>a new melody he just wrote.</i>

00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:27.400
It reached him.

00:17:28.050 --> 00:17:29.270
It really did.

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:35.440
<i>Out of all the times I've sung until now,</i>

00:17:36.890 --> 00:17:39.780
<i>this is the melody that 
melts my heart the most.</i>

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:55.180
Nino?

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:58.410
<i>There's no way that was Momo.</i>

00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:03.840
<i>If Momo was here, he would have come 
to see me before anything else.</i>

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:07.250
<i>So it wasn't him.</i>

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:09.020
<i>It still hasn't reached him.</i>

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:12.180
<i>If singing like that won't reach him...</i>

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:16.370
<i>I don't know what I should do anymore.</i>

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:25.490
No punishment from the student council!
The club won't be shut down!

00:18:25.490 --> 00:18:28.500
Everyone thought the part where Nino-chan 
forgot the lyrics was part of the show

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:30.620
and got really into it.

00:18:31.030 --> 00:18:32.590
<i>The way Alice looked yesterday</i>

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:37.340
<i>was just like back then.</i>

00:18:39.190 --> 00:18:40.660
Yuzu-kun?

00:18:42.060 --> 00:18:45.760
I want to go thank Nino-chan.

00:18:45.760 --> 00:18:47.480
Alice is absent today.

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:49.690
Huh? Why? Is she sick?

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:53.360
How should I know? Didn't I tell 
you I don't care about her?!

00:18:53.360 --> 00:19:00.610
Totally cares

00:18:54.410 --> 00:18:56.670
The "I care" is just oozing off of him, though...

00:18:56.670 --> 00:19:00.610
He should really worry about his 
personality more than his height.

00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:05.660
But really, her voice was 
beyond what I had imagined.

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:08.720
I can tell tell why Yuzu-kun's 
so captivated by that canary.

00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:14.010
Hey, Yuzuriha-kun, are you 
a fan of In NO Hurry, too?

00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:17.130
You did a cover of <i>High School</i>
at orientation, didn't you?

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:18.660
Yeah.

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:20.240
In NO Hurry is great, huh?

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:21.050
Yeah.

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:24.090
Arisugawa-san's singing was amazing, too!

00:19:24.090 --> 00:19:26.180
Yeah, I totally had goosebumps!

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:28.330
Her singing voice is so cool.

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:31.230
Yeah! I want to hear her 
sing some other songs!

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:32.290
Damn it!

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:34.670
Yana-chan, did you listen to it?

00:19:34.670 --> 00:19:35.480
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:19:38.460 --> 00:19:40.490
This voice is pretty interesting.

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:43.370
I like it.

00:19:45.110 --> 00:19:46.150
Miou.

00:19:47.340 --> 00:19:49.180
What were you up to yesterday?

00:19:49.180 --> 00:19:52.160
I seriously can't believe you 
skipped out on the concert.

00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:54.750
Sorry. But I really didn't want to do it.

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:55.630
Why not?

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:59.510
Obviously, because the real Alice is here now.

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:02.940
I'm done pretending to be Alice.

00:20:02.940 --> 00:20:03.870
Miou...

00:20:04.490 --> 00:20:08.280
Yuzu never even gave me the 
time of day to begin with.

00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:10.140
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:13.400
You should give up on Yuzu 
and be my girl instead.

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:18.730
No matter how many times 
I hear it, that joke's hilarious!

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:21.400
I know, right? Cheers you right up, doesn't it?

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:24.710
Yeah, I feel much better. 
Thanks, Haruyoshi-senpai!

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:32.510
A joke, huh?

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:40.200
What a coincidence!

00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:44.160
Yuzu.

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:48.430
I just happened to have something 
I needed to do out here.

00:20:49.450 --> 00:20:51.180
I've been singing here since morning.

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:54.180
Huh? It's already past noon.

00:20:54.840 --> 00:20:56.560
During the concert...

00:20:56.990 --> 00:20:59.780
I thought I heard Momo's voice.

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:01.780
Nino?

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:04.900
But it wasn't him.

00:21:05.970 --> 00:21:08.530
The only Momo I know is from six years ago.

00:21:09.390 --> 00:21:11.310
It had to be my imagination.

00:21:13.340 --> 00:21:14.750
It was just my imagination,

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:16.740
but I really...

00:21:18.780 --> 00:21:21.590
I really didn't want to think 
it was just my imagination.

00:21:22.410 --> 00:21:24.280
So I couldn't stop singing.

00:21:25.570 --> 00:21:29.140
<i>I felt like I was just so close to reaching him.</i>

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:34.780
I still like Momo.

00:21:37.220 --> 00:21:37.910
Yeah.

00:21:42.220 --> 00:21:45.030
I'll write more songs, so why not sing them?

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:51.790
I'll make you more songs for 
when you feel like screaming.

00:21:52.980 --> 00:21:54.860
So you can sing without 
worrying about anything.

00:21:56.550 --> 00:22:01.530
<i>At that time, I prayed for the 
same thing, over and over again.</i>

00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:05.190
Didn't I tell you?

00:22:05.750 --> 00:22:07.840
If you sing believing you'll 
see him again, you will.

00:22:09.210 --> 00:22:10.180
It'll be fine.

00:22:11.090 --> 00:22:11.990
You'll see him again.

00:22:12.270 --> 00:22:13.660
<i>I hope she never sees him.</i>

00:22:14.400 --> 00:22:17.370
<i>I hope she never sees Momo again.</i>

00:22:18.310 --> 00:22:21.930
So how about we go to school?

00:22:29.010 --> 00:22:31.030
Thanks, Yuzu.

00:22:32.800 --> 00:22:33.850
<i>God,</i>

00:22:34.940 --> 00:22:36.440
<i>I pray that Alice's love</i>

00:22:38.260 --> 00:22:41.990
<i>will never be realized.</i>

00:23:47.030 --> 00:23:52.240
♭03 
Whatever It Takes, Right Now
